# Docstrings over comments

Document contracts in **docstrings** (module, class, function). Do not rely on
narrative `#` comments.

## Do

- Put API invariants, fail-closed behavior, detector order, and pack semantics in
  module or function docstrings.
- Prefer clear names and tests over explaining what the next lines do.
- Keep `# type: ignore[...]` and other required toolchain directives.

## Don't

- Narrate code (`# scrub the email`, `# loop detectors`).
- Duplicate the docstring beside the implementation.
- Leave "why" only in a `#` above a regex or branch when a docstring on the
  function/module can hold it.

## Rare exception

A one-line `#` is OK only when the code looks wrong but isn't and a docstring
cannot sit at that exact site (true footgun). Prefer a named helper or test
instead when practical.

```python
# ❌ BAD
# Prefer model_copy when available (pydantic); else rebuild TextContent.
if hasattr(block, "model_copy"):
    ...

# ✅ GOOD — behavior obvious from control flow; contract lives on the module/fn
if hasattr(block, "model_copy"):
    ...
```
